The attached image displays confocal microscopy images of skeletal muscle injection sites 24 hours post-injection, illustrating Nano-11 uptake and inflammatory cell recruitment, as presented in Figure 10 of the 2015 article. The top row shows significant infiltration of Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages (green) and MHCII+ cells (green), with intracellular localization of AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) when co-injected with ovalbumin (OVA). This indicates efficient phagocytosis of Nano-11 by these cell types. In contrast, the bottom row, representing soluble OVA injection, shows minimal cellular infiltration and no Nano-11, demonstrating Nano-11's role in localizing the adjuvant and recruiting immune cells.